<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Oct real retail sales rise 14.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Czech Oct real retail sales rise 14.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech October retail sales, in real terms, rose 14.7 percent compared with the same month in 1995, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The CSU also said that total internal trade rose by 14.2 percent year-on-year in real terms in October.</p>
<p> CZECH REAL RETAIL SALES	OCT 96   SEPT 96   JAN-OCT 96</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +14.7    +12.7	 +9.3</p>
<p>CZECH REAL INTERNAL TRADE</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +14.2    +13.8	+11.6</p>
<p>Note: All figures are preliminary. Total internal trade includes retail sales plus sales and repairs of motor cars, motor fuel, restaurant services and accommodation.  </p>
<p>The CSU also gave the following real retail sales data (percentage change year-on-year):</p>
<p>				     OCT 96   SEPT 96  JAN-OCT 96</p>
<p>sales, repairs of motor</p>
<p> vehicles plus motor fuel     16.1	22.9     24.5</p>
<p>restaurants and</p>
<p> accommodation		     6.1	 5.7	6.9</p>
<p>TRANSPORT</p>
<p>  total				5.7	 5.1     13.6</p>
<p>  railways			  10.7	 1.9	4.1</p>
<p>  road transport		  -2.4	 4.1	9.9</p>
<p>  river			     37.1     -20.1    -22.6</p>
<p>  air				-19.5	-2.8     -3.1</p>
<p>parallel and support</p>
<p>  activities			26.8	11.2     32.7</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in positive terms except where denoted.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
